              <div class="content-middle">
            <div class="region region-content">
    <div id="block-danland-fremontco-purple-brighter-system-main" class="block">
  
      <h2 class="block-title"><span>Front Page</span>
</h2>
    
  <div class="content">
          <article data-history-node-id="3622" class="node node--type-page node--view-mode-full">

  
    

  
    <div class="content">
      
            <div><h1>County Notices:</h1>
<p><div class="front-page-notices js-view-dom-id-c5654a6651a8f02878fa52b3f1d77d934d5f2c0a9f5c81876a250f5e56d72b33">
  
  
  

  
  
  

      <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><h2 class="field-content">Extended Road Closure Notice 9/14/2026 - 9/17/2026</h2></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content"><p>The Fremont County DOT will be continuing roadwork on Shelf Road from MM10 thru MM14. The road will be closed to all traffic from Monday September 14, 2026 thru Thursday September 17, 2026 while crews continue to repair damage from rain events.</p>
<p>The road will be open this Friday, Saturday, and Sunday (September 11-13), and will be open next Friday, Saturday, and Sunday (September 18-20). Detours will be in place alerting all traveling public. Feel free to share this information with anyone who may need it, and plan accordingly for your commute. Thank you for your patience and cooperation while our crews work to complete the needed repairs.</p>
</div></div><div class="views-field views-field-edit-node"><span class="field-content"></span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-date-posted"><div class="field-content"><time datetime="2026-09-10T12:00:00Z">September  10,  2026</time>

<hr></div></div></div>
    <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><h2 class="field-content">Veteran Services Office Closure</h2></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content"><p>The Veteran Services Office will be closed starting on October 6th. It will reopen on October 12th.</p>
</div></div><div class="views-field views-field-edit-node"><span class="field-content"></span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-date-posted"><div class="field-content"><time datetime="2026-09-08T12:00:00Z">September  8,  2026</time>

<hr></div></div></div>
    <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><h2 class="field-content">Fremont County Airport 2026 Fly-In &amp; Drive-In</h2></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content"><p>Start your day with aviation, automobiles, and community fun at our annual Fly-In &amp; Drive-In! Join pilots, aviation enthusiasts, classic car owners, and community members on Saturday, September 26, 2026, from 7:30 A.M. to 11:00 A.M. at the Fremont County Airport.</p>
<p>Enjoy a delicious pancake breakfast while exploring a variety of aircraft and vehicles on display. Browse unique items at our fly-market, connect with fellow aviators and enthusiasts, and experience our favorite annual event.</p>
<p>Whether you’re flying in, driving in, or simply looking for a fun Saturday morning outing, there’s something for everyone to enjoy. &nbsp;For event details or fly market vendor registration, please visit our Facebook page or contact the Airport Office at 719-784-3816.</p>
<p>We look forward to seeing you at the airport!</p>
</div></div><div class="views-field views-field-edit-node"><span class="field-content"></span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-date-posted"><div class="field-content"><time datetime="2026-09-03T12:00:00Z">September  3,  2026</time>

<hr></div></div></div>
    <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><h2 class="field-content">2026 Fremont County Airport Fly-In and Drive-In</h2></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content"><p>Start your day with aviation, automobiles, and community fun at our annual Fly-In &amp; Drive-In! Join pilots, aviation enthusiasts, classic car owners, and community members on Saturday, September 26, 2026, from 7:30 A.M. to 11:00 A.M. at the Fremont County Airport.</p>
<p>Enjoy a delicious pancake breakfast while exploring a variety of aircraft and vehicles on display. Browse unique items at our fly-market, connect with fellow aviators and enthusiasts, and experience our favorite annual event.</p>
<p>Whether you’re flying in, driving in, or simply looking for a fun Saturday morning outing, there’s something for everyone to enjoy.</p>
<p>For event details or fly market vendor registration, please visit our Facebook page or contact the Airport Office at 719-784-3816.</p>
<p>We look forward to seeing you at the airport!</p>
</div></div><div class="views-field views-field-edit-node"><span class="field-content"></span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-date-posted"><div class="field-content"><time datetime="2026-07-28T12:00:00Z">July  28,  2026</time>

<hr></div></div></div>

    

  
  

  
  
</div>
</p>
</div>
      
    </div>

</article>

      </div>
</div>

  </div>

        </div>
      
      
    </div> <!-- end content -->

